-- #1111 A-2.12 (#1319 unit 2) — the FIELD→OWNERS half, on all three engines.
--
-- `universeFieldOwners` is the one member of `registerRecordInfoKeyed`'s write site
-- that A-2.6's overlay structurally could not reach: it is an ACCUMULATING multimap,
-- so an imported record's owner is added BESIDE an unimported one, never over it.
-- The key (the field name) was never wrong; the candidate SET was graph-global.
--
-- Before: `usef` was REJECTED, exit 1, `Ambiguous field access: '.shared' is
-- declared by FA, FB; the record type is undetermined` — where `FB` is a record
-- `usef` has no import path to and cannot spell, so even the suggested annotation is
-- unactionable.  Measured on a binary cold-built from `main` @ 1443870c.
--
-- Expected output, derived BY HAND before any capture:
--   rf   = getf mkFA + bf 0                                  = 3 + 0  = 3
--   bysf = getMine (URec { mine = 4, … }) + mkFA.onlyA       = 4 + 1  = 5
-- so `3`, `5`.
import usef.{rf}
import bystandf.{bysf}

main : <IO> Unit
main =
  let _ = putStrLn (intToString rf)
  putStrLn (intToString bysf)
